<title>ITALY: Italian plan, with welfare outlines, ready end-May.</title>
<headline>Italian plan, with welfare outlines, ready end-May.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian government's 1998-200 economic programme (DPEF) will be ready at the end of May and will contain broad outlines of planned social welfare reforms, Labour Minister Tiziano Treu said.</p>
<p>The document of economic targets for the next three years &quot;will contain the strategic outlines of welfare state reform,&quot; Treu told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;It will show clearly where we want to go as regards pensions,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
